Methods of the Sensors of the Tank
Plant Simulation Help 11-2785
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

createSensor [SimTalk] - Tank
Creates a new sensor for the Tank designated by <Path>.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.createSensor([Position:real, Control:method, Exceeded:boolean, 
Underrun:boolean, PositionType:string]) → integer
Parameters
The sensor itself is defined by these parameters:
• The optional parameter Position of data type real sets the relative position.
• The optional parameter Control of data type method designates the name of the Method object that the
sensor triggers.
You can specify the name of the method as a string, i.e., "myMethod" or you can specify &myMethod.
• The optional parameter Exceeded of data type boolean sets if the sensor is going to be triggered when
the amount of material in the Tank has exceeded, i.e., is located above the sensor position (true) or not
(false).
• The optional parameter Underrun of data type boolean sets if the sensor is going to be triggered once
the amount of material in the Tank has underrun, i.e., is located below the sensor position (true) or not
(false).
• The optional parameter PositionType of data type string designates the position type of the sensor:
Relative or Absolute.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
It is the unique number of the sensor. You can use this number to access the sensor.
Example
var ID1,ID2: integer
ID1 := MyTank.createSensor(0.5,"SensorCtrl",true,false)
ID2 := MyTank.createSensor(0.7,&myMethod,false,true)
ID3 := MyTank.createSensor(3,"SensorCtrl",true,false,"absolute")
